    "problem": "$\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
    "worked_solution": "Factoring out the constant $\\frac{1}{2}$ and calculating the resulting integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
